{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a8f3-c96c-76f0-b402-07e24facc60e"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cf0d70f9-80e9-40d1-b7e2-9ab1aef0f049","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cf0d70f9-80e9-40d1-b7e2-9ab1aef0f049","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cf0d70f9-80e9-40d1-b7e2-9ab1aef0f049"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a8f4-3f9a-7121-8539-331f6ff47399"},"task_id":"01a0a8f4-3f9a-7121-8539-331f6ff47399","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a8f4-3f9a-7121-8539-331f6ff47399","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/outputs/RunnerControl/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260916-13diw4/TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v5.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-13diw4: register-mac-and-repository-access — developer outcome v5\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`, uncommitted candidate in story worktree).\n4|\n5|This run implements BOTH revision-4 findings (R4-F1 + R4-F2,\n6|`changes_requested`, `repeat-of: revision 3 / R3-F1` for both) as one coherent\n7|operation-owner + directory-lease lifecycle change per the revision-5 contract,\n8|adopting the reviewer's exact attack source as committed named regressions.\n9|Prior M1–M27 regions were not rerun per contract (unchanged code); the M9\n10|survivor bound is restated from v3.\n11|\n12|## Fixes (code)\n13|\n14|1. **R4-F1 — abandoned completion released a still-running directory mutation\n15|   (repeat-of R3-F1).** New per-directory lease in `RunnerInstallerService`:\n16|   `activeDirectories` set acquired synchronously before the first await in\n17|   `downloadAndInstall` and `runConfig` (resume/reuse checks included) and\n18|   released via `defer` only when the owning side effect settles. `setupService`\n19|   and `recoverPartialInstall` refuse via `requireIdleDirectory` while a live\n20|   async side effect owns the directory. Conflicts throw the new retryable\n21|   `RegistrationError.directoryBusy`; different directories never conflict.\n22|   Abandoning a UI generation does not release the lease.\n23|2. **R4-F2 — stale failure cleared the current operation's busy guard\n24|   (repeat-of R3-F1).** `Flow.working: Bool` replaced with\n25|   `workingOwner: Int?` (owning generation, nil when idle). Every step sets the\n26|   owner before its first await; `fail` and `finishStep` are now\n27|   generation-owned (`guard workingOwner == gen`), and all seven catch blocks\n28|   lost their unconditional `working = false`. A stale success/failure/cancel\n29|   exit mutates nothing: no lock release, no step clear, no planted failedStep.\n30|   `beginDraft`/`updateDraft`/`cancel`/`reset` hand the UI lock to the new\n31|   generation at once while live side effects keep their leases.\n32|\n33|## AC coverage — 8 of 8 rows driven through production entry points\n34|\n35|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n36||---|--------|-------------------------|----------------------|\n37|| 1 | Org registration without terminal | `orgWizardEndToEndDeletesTokenAndLeaksNothing`, `reviewerInFlightInstallCannotRepopulateChangedDraft`, `reviewerRetryCannotRunTwoConfigsInSameDirectory`, `cancelDuringConfigKeepsLeaseAndRecoversAfterSettle` | `Flow.apply` (.beginDraft/.resolveGroup/.downloadAndInstall/.registerRunner/.setupService/.retry/.cancel) |\n38|| 2 | Repo registration without terminal | `repoWizardOmitsRunnerGroup`, `repoRunnerListRequestUsesQueryNotEncodedPath` | same Flow effects; no `runner-groups` traffic, no `--runnergroup` argv |\n39|| 3 | Selected repos are applied | `orgResolveGroupCreatesWithSelectedRepos`, `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs`, `repositoryConfirmationFollowsPagination`, `inFlightAccessAbandonedWhenRepositoriesEdited` | `createGroup` / `setGroupRepositories` + paginated `fetchGroupRepositories` confirm |\n40|| 4 | Repo access and labels changeable | `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs`, `labelsApplyRequiresRealRunnerIDThenPuts`, `inFlightLabelsAbandonedWhenLabelsEdited` | `Flow.apply(.applyRepositoryAccess/.applyLabels)` with verified IDs |\n41|| 5 | Failed ops avoid orphans | `failedConfigDeletesTokenAndReportsScrubbedError`, `registerIsIdempotentAcrossRetries`, `registerRefusesMismatchedRemoteIdentity`, `cancelDuringConfigKeepsLeaseAndRecoversAfterSettle` (both tokens deleted) | `Flow.registerRunner` (token deleted on every failure path; single mint/config) |\n42|| 6 | Repeated ops avoid duplicates | `registerIsIdempotentAcrossRetries`, `retryResumesFailedDownloadWithoutDuplicates`, `remoteDuplicateWithoutReplaceIsRefusedBeforeToken`, `runnerListFollowsPaginationForDuplicateGuard`, `existingRegistrationBlocksFreshInstall`, `reviewerRetryCannotRunTwoConfigsInSameDirectory` (1 config call), `beginDraftDuringDownloadKeepsDirectoryLease`, `resetDuringDownloadKeepsDirectoryLeaseUntilSettled`, `nonconflictingInstallProceedsWhileOtherDirectoryRuns` (scope control) | complete-list `rejectRemoteDuplicate` gate + installer markers + directory lease + owner lock |\n43|| 7 | No secret leakage | `orgWizardEndToEndDeletesTokenAndLeaksNothing`, `runConfigScrubsTokenFromFailure`, `failedConfigDeletesTokenAndReportsScrubbedError`, `cancelDuringConfigKeepsLeaseAndRecoversAfterSettle` | token only in config.sh argv in memory; absent from actions/URLs/headers/bodies; deleted after use |\n44|| 8 | Tests exercise actual entry points | all Flow tests + `setupServiceWritesManualPlistFoundByDiscovery`, `runConfigExecutesRealScript`, `staleRegisterFailureDoesNotUnlockOrPlantFailure`, `scopeChangeClearsCompletedStepsInState` | `Flow.apply`, `RunnerInstallerService.*`, `State.reduce`, cross-checked by `RunnerDiscovery.installed` and a real shell `config.sh` |\n45|\n46|Negative/refusal coverage (each fails when the gate admits what it must\n47|reject): all v3/v4 negatives retained and green, plus the two adopted reviewer\n48|attacks and five new R5 lifecycle tests (`beginDraft…`, `reset…`, `cancel…`,\n49|`nonconflicting…` scope control, `staleRegisterFailure…` cross-step control).\n50|\n51|## Narrowing-mutant evidence (this run, each reverted pristine via sha256)\n52|\n53|New/changed gates only (M1–M27 unchanged regions not rerun per contract):\n54|\n55|| Mutant | Admits exactly | Named failing test(s) | Result |\n56||--------|----------------|-----------------------|--------|\n57|| M28: `fail` guard `workingOwner == gen \\|\\| step == \"downloadAndInstall\"` | stale download-failure unlocks only | `reviewerStaleFailureCannotUnlockNewOperation` (1 issue: after 2 vs before 1) | KILLED, exit 1; control `staleRegisterFailureDoesNotUnlockOrPlantFailure` (register stale class) passes |\n58|| M29: `runConfig` lease acquire/release skipped | same-directory overlapping config only | `reviewerRetryCannotRunTwoConfigsInSameDirectory` (2 issues: 2 config calls; attested-complete vs .runner mismatch) | KILLED, exit 1; control `beginDraftDuringDownloadKeepsDirectoryLease` (download lease class) passes |\n59|\n60|No survivors in M28–M29. Prior M9 (`createGroup` default true→false)\n61|survivor bound restated from v3 (unchanged code, not rerun): the default is\n62|not load-bearing, Flow passes `true` explicitly, M9b kills the call site.\n63|\n64|The source-text-token mutant rule does not apply: no gate inspects source\n65|text.\n66|\n67|## Verification commands (real exit codes)\n68|\n69|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` (CI gate):\n70|  **exit 0, 154 tests passed** (147 + 2 adopted + 5 new R5), re-run green after\n71|  mutant revert with pristine sha256 match on both touched sources.\n72|- `python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests` (CI gate): **exit 0,\n73|  4 tests OK**.\n74|- `xcodebuild -workspace RunnerControl.xcworkspace -scheme RunnerControl\n75|  -destination 'platform=macOS' build`: **BUILD SUCCEEDED** (exit 0).\n76|- No repo-configured lint gate (CI runs only the two test jobs above;\n77|  no `.swiftlint.yml`).\n78|- Generator inputs untouched: `ios-app-manager.json`, `Project.swift`,\n79|  `Workspace.swift`, `Package.swift` unmodified (no new source files added);\n80|  existing production runners untouched (all test IO under temp roots;\n81|  services never bootstrapped); candidate left UNCOMMITTED, no producer commit.\n82|\n83|## Files changed (all UNCOMMITTED in story worktree, as required)\n84|\n85|- `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/RunnerRegistration+Models.swift` —\n86|  retryable `directoryBusy(path:)` error.\n87|- `…/RunnerInstallerService.swift` — `activeDirectories` lease registry,\n88|  `leaseKey`/`acquireLease`/`releaseLease`/`requireIdleDirectory`, integrated\n89|  into `downloadAndInstall`, `runConfig`, `setupService`,\n90|  `recoverPartialInstall`.\n91|- `…/RunnerRegistration+Flow.swift` — `workingOwner` operation lock,\n92|  generation-owned `fail`/`finishStep`, owner set/guard in all seven steps,\n93|  `retry` guard, `beginDraft`/`updateDraft`/`cancel`/`reset` handoff; all seven\n94|  unconditional catch clears removed.\n95|- `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Tests/RunnerRegistrationTests.swift` — 2\n96|  verbatim reviewer regressions + `ReviewTwoDownloads` + 5 R5 lifecycle tests,\n97|  `CountingLatchDownloader`, `ConfigLatchExecutor` failure injection.\n98|\n99|## Stated bounds (unknowns, not guesses)\n100|\n101|- Live registration smoke remains a separate delivery task; transport covered\n102|  by fakes, filesystem by temp-root fixtures with real `tar`/`shasum`/`config.sh`.\n103|- Authenticated download `sha256_checksum` availability was confirmed\n104|  nonempty for osx x64/arm64 by root read-only live API (per revision-4\n105|  contract); this run made no live GitHub calls.\n106|- Pagination cap is 100 pages per list (fail-closed throw, never silent\n107|  partial).\n108|- Mid-step session change is bound by single-auth reuse (no mixing); an\n109|  inter-step change invalidates via `syncServerBinding` plus `.runner`/marker\n110|  verification.\n111|- Ownership table stays per-Mac (`~/Library/GitHubActions/\n112|  .runnercontrol-groups.json`); two local users do not share it. Pre-revision-4\n113|  ownership entries (no server) and configured markers (no group) fail closed\n114|  toward explicit takeover/reconfiguration, never silent adoption.\n115|- A same-directory retry refused with `directoryBusy` mints and deletes a\n116|  short-lived registration token for the register step before reaching the\n117|  lease; the token is never used for a second config and never retained.","final_result":true}}}
